[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Document Databases and BSON/JSON Internals"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Document databases represent a paradigm shift from traditional relational database management systems by storing data as flexible, semi-structured documents. Understanding how these databases handle data serialization formats like JSON and its binary counterpart, BSON, is crucial for optimizing performance, schema design, and storage efficiency."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"The JSON Data Model and Its Limitations"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) is the lingua franca of web applications and document databases due to its human-readable syntax and native compatibility with JavaScript. A standard JSON document consists of attribute-value pairs and ordered lists of values."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"{
